t me search the enemy ID array more carefully: In the stretches, I saw values only 0 and 6. So no.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider the 1-1 enemy list from ROM. Actually, let me try decoding the ROM list with the *actual* SMB format which I can derive by fitting the known Goomba positions.\n\nKnown: Goombas at ~1395? Let me use the two Goombas we saw at screen 138/162 with Mario at 1475: their level x = 1533 and 1557.\n\nAlso, at the last screenshot Mario at 2850 with a Goomba at screen x≈30: hmm, the camera would be at 2850-118 = 2732; the Goomba at screen 30 → 2762.\n\nAnd earlier: Goombas at ~2110 (behind Mario) → around 2100; at 2570 (the one at screen 30 in the staircase screenshot? that was at x≈2594, Goomba behind at screen 30 → ~2506?).\n\nHmm, these are approximate.\n\nLet me try to decode the ROM list assuming 3-byte records with byte0 = x_page:y? The mapping's claim: \"byte0 = x-page:y nibbles\". So byte0's high nibble = x page, low nibble = y? and byte1 = \"flags/within-page\" (the x within the page), byte2 = enemy type.\n\nTest: (1E,C2,00): x page = 1, y = $E? x within page = $C2 = 194 → x = 256+194 = 450? Hmm, the first Goomba in 1-1 is at x≈352... Hmm, but actually the first Goomba might be at 450? Hmm. Actually, hmm: the first Goomba in 1-1 comes right after the first ? block area, around x= 350-450. Plausible!\n\nNext (6B,06,8B): page 6, within $06 → x = 1536+6 = 1542. Our Goombas at 1533/1557! Close to 1542! \n\nNext (86,63,B7): page 8, within $63=99 → x = 2048+99 = 2147. Hmm, we saw Goombas around 2100-2150. Plausible!\n\nThen PAGE(0F,05): page entry — sets the \"current page\" to 5? Then (03,06,23): hmm.\n\nHmm, this is promising but the byte1 values (C2, 06, 63, 06, 4B, 00, FB, B7, 1B) as \"within page\" are odd (some > 255, no they're bytes). Hmm, byte1 $C2 = 194, $06 = 6, $63 = 99, $06, $4B = 75, $00, $FB=251, $B7=183, $1B=27.\n\nAnd byte2 = enemy type: 00, 8B, B7, 23, B7, 5B, 37, 0F, 37. Hmm, those don't look like enemy types.\n\nHmm, so maybe the t