ites at slots 28-30 ARE the flag (3 OAM entries). Hmm, so the flag is drawn by the flagpole object's sprite routine. Let me check: tile $7E/$7F in palette 5.\n\nHmm, but the rendered flag at (228,50) is white/light gray — palette 5 live = [$0F,$1A green,$30 white,$27 orange]? From the mapping: \"Sprite palette 5 live = [15,26,48,39] = [$0F,$1A,$30,$27]\" — hmm, that was for the fire flower in 1-1. Palette 5 slot 2 = $30 white → the flag renders white. ✓.\n\nSo the flag is a sprite with tiles $7E/$7F, palette 5, at the top of the pole. \n\nHmm, and it seems to be 3 entries: (216,49) tile $7E, (224,49) tile $7F, (224,57) tile $7E. The visible flag in the screenshot is at (225-240, 45-60) — a white triangle. Hmm, so the flag sprite is ~16x16 at (216,49)-(231,64)? But the screenshot shows the flag as a triangle pointing left, at the right of the pole.\n\nHmm, but hold on: the task says to find the flagpole and its flag: \"get_region in object mode on the pole and on the flag (the proof); record each CHR tile of the pole and its top ball ... and the flag (it may be a sprite)\".\n\nSo: the pole and its top ball are BACKGROUND tiles; the flag is a SPRITE. \n\nNow let me:\n1. get_region object mode on the pole (a background tile) → get the CHR tiles.\n2. get_region object mode on the flag (a sprite pixel) → but get_region works on rendered pixels by palette slot; for a sprite it should work too.\n3. get_tile_at_pixel on the pole at several heights to get the pole's CHR tiles (shaft + ball).\n4. record_mapping for the pole tiles and the flag sprite.\n\nBut FIRST: the Koopa! Where is it? The task requires recording the Koopa Troopa. Hmm, we're at the flagpole and no Koopa Troopa has appeared.\n\nWAIT. Hmm! Maybe the \"Koopa Troopa\" in 1-1... Let me reconsider. In 1-1, is there really a Koopa Troopa? Let me think hard. \n\nActually — YES. In World 1-1 of SMB, there IS a Koopa Troopa: it's on the flat area just before the staircase? Hmm, no. Let me think about the level again: