atched, and screenshot each stretch. The Koopa must show up.\n\nWait, hmm, actually: maybe the Koopa is a \"falling\" enemy? No.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider: \"A Koopa Troopa and more Little Goombas appear.\" — the Koopa Troopa walks on the ground. In our run, at x≈2400-2600 we saw... hmm, at x=2594 the screenshot showed a pipe at x≈125-155 and a Goomba at screen 30 (behind Mario). Hmm.\n\nHmm, wait! Maybe the Koopa Troopa IS the enemy I saw at x≈2762 in the screenshot at x=2850 (the \"Goomba behind at (30,205)\")? Hmm, that looked brown = Goomba.\n\nHmm. OK, let me just continue. Two more stretches should cover 2162→2500.\n\nActually, to speed up: let me use a 120-frame stretch with jumps, watching flags+IDs, then screenshot.\n\nHmm, but Mario stalls at the staircase steps. The stairs need jumps.\n\nLet me do: [{right,b,a}20,{right,b}10] × 4 = 120 frames.\n\nLet me also include the watch of $0014 (flag slot5) → addresses 15,16,17,18,19,20 (flags 0-5) + 22,23,24,25,26,27 (IDs) = 12 addresses. OK.\n\nGo."}
